// Sword reach, one point of the sweep over distance (160 / 230 / 260 / 300 uu between the pawns'
// centres, straight ahead, victim facing the attacker so no assassination). Rule (research/dishonored/systems/melee.md):
// the swing context's m_fMaxContextRange is 210 x max(Attribute_Range, 1); the sweep (m_fSweepingAttackSize 60)
// reaches the first body. The port tests a 210 uu segment from the eye against the victim's axis with a
// 30 uu tolerance on top of the 35 uu radius, i.e. centres up to about 275 uu apart.
// Expected hit below is the design reading (centre distance <= reach + collision radius = 245): UNMEASURED.
(
    name: "combat/melee_reach_d160",
    system: Combat,
    map: "Playground",
    description: "One swing at a passive guard 160 uu straight ahead: does it connect.",
    setup: (
        player: Some((position: (-5300, 0, 96), yaw: 180, pitch: -5)),
        npcs: [(id: Some("dummy"), position: Some((-5460, 0, 92)), yaw: 0, state: Some("Passive"))],
        settle: 30,
    ),
    ticks: 120,
    input: [(tick: 5, action: Press(Primary))],
    checkpoints: [
        (name: "connects", expect: [(metric: Count("Sim:Damage@dummy"), value: 1, tol: 0, source: "reach 210 from the eye + body radius 35 (melee.md); the port reaches about 275", status: Unmeasured)]),
    ],
    record: [Pawn, Npc("dummy"), SimEvents],
    capture: Some("measure sword npc=<placed guard> --swings 1 at distance 160 (lab place); record the damage-path call or none"),
)